   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>I want an observer which suspends itself. The most obvious way to do this is to save a reference to the observer:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">test </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> observe</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(..</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stuff</span><span style=\"color:#660\">..)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    test$suspend</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><code><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(..</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stuff</span><span style=\"color:#660\">..)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></code><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>Is it possible to do this without the reference? I&#39;m thinking of something like this$suspend().<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
